From: ACK72 <acikom72@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:50:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: keep IPv6 flow source MAC slots immutable

Redesign the source-MAC allocation from Gilly 972/973 as one change.
Allocate IPv6 GDM egress MACs from slots 5..14, never the mutable GDM
base slots or KEEP slot 15. Serialize both words and check write ACKs.
Share exact MAC matches but never recycle programmed slots until full
hardware initialization. Thus flow-delete failures and in-flight packets
cannot observe a reassigned MAC. Exhaustion or write failure declines
offload. Failed writes quarantine their slot. No MAC addresses are logged.

This deliberately bounds hardware offload to ten distinct GDM IPv6 egress
MACs per hardware lifetime; subsequent MACs use software forwarding.
L2 KEEP, Wi-Fi egress and inline IPv4 MAC handling retain their behavior.

Adapted-from: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott@hotmail.com>, patches 972 and 973
Source: https://github.com/Gilly1970/Gemtek-W1700K-6.18/tree/4b8fb8c3a2619dd239fb44fd511ee2848a07e768/openwrt-patches

diff --git a/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/9999-z-airoha-ipv6-source-mac-slots.patch b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/9999-z-airoha-ipv6-source-mac-slots.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
